# GitHub production mirror

- Public publish target: `production/agentic-orchestration-quill` (submodule → `zlatko-lakisic/agentic-orchestration-quill`).
- Mirror **tracked** parent files only. Exclude `production/` and `.gitmodules`.
- Never copy `production/` into the submodule — that nests the submodule inside itself.

## Release flow

1. Sync tracked files (minus `production/`, `.gitmodules`) into the submodule.
2. Commit in the submodule on `main`.
3. Annotated tag `vX.Y.Z`, push branch + tag.
4. `gh release create vX.Y.Z` on the code repo.
5. Update the parent submodule pointer on a feature branch and open a PR (never commit straight to `main`).

## Twin wiki

`ao-quill.wiki` mirrors the same way into `production/agentic-orchestration-quill.wiki`. Tag and push only — GitHub wiki remotes do not support `gh release`.
